    "result_text": "The build is green: **50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked everything that keys off the household, all in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (plus doc updates in `openapi.yml`).\n\n**Core change \u2014 `householdIdFor(lastName, postcode)`**\n- Now computes the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, where `normalizedLastName` is the existing collapsed (trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/lower-cased) form and a `null` postcode collapses to empty. Previously it hashed `lastName + '\\n' + address` and prefixed `HH-`.\n- `assignHouseholdId` now feeds `postcode` instead of `address`, so owners sharing `(lastName, postcode)` automatically get the same id \u2014 and `householdMemberCount` (which reads `getHouseholdId()`) follows for free, including the household-size input to membership level.\n\n**Duplicate detection**\n- `identityKeyFor` now folds in the postcode-based `householdId` (signature changed from address\u2192postcode), keeping the identity-key collision check (409) intact \u2014 this is why a full duplicate with `sharesHousehold=true` still collides (Cp28).\n- Added `rejectDuplicateHousehold`: a second owner whose computed `householdId` already exists is rejected with 409 (`DuplicateHouseholdException`, already wired to a 409 handler), **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member. `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses this block, not the identity check.\n\n**Possible-duplicate flag**\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` now takes a `declaredHouseholdMember` flag; a declared member (opted in via `sharesHousehold`) is never flagged as a suspected duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`), satisfying Cp35's \"declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions/examples for `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, and `identityKey` to reflect the new `(lastName, postcode)` derivation.",
